@@ -0,0 +1,937 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project
+"""Prefill sequence parallelism (SP) for DeepSeek V4.1 tensor parallelism.
+
+## Mode
+
+At tensor parallel size N every rank repeats the row-wise work of a decoder
+layer (mHC mixes, norms, the Engram gate, the residual carry) on every token.
+For a long prefill forward, SP turns the per-layer all-reduces into dim-0
+reduce-scatters so that each rank owns 1/N of the rows for that work, and
+all-gathers the rows back before the ops that need all of them. Weights stay
+exactly as in ordinary TP, except that each compressor layer (the CED
+boundary's ratio one, the encoder's ratio two) retains one full BF16
+compressor weight for its local-row projection. The static
+``_use_sequence_parallel`` construction flag stays off: this mode changes no
+module.
+
+SP trades two all-gathers per layer for reduce-scatters that split the
+row-wise work across the ranks, so a forward runs sequence-parallel exactly
+when that trade can pay; there is no setting. It must be prompt processing:
+decode forwards (at most the largest CUDA graph capture size, and at most
+``max_num_seqs * (1 + num_speculative_tokens)`` tokens) replay captured
+graphs and keep full rows. And its reduce-scatter must really scatter: a
+conservative hidden-state byte threshold comes from the TP group's
+registered one-shot RoCE capacity. This preserves the qualified SP boundary
+when transport dispatch is tuned independently below that capacity. It is
+a performance policy, not a claim that every smaller message uses RoCE.
+``DeepseekV4Model.forward`` decides per forward from the token count T,
+which every rank shares, so no agreement between ranks is needed. SP is off
+only where it cannot apply: tensor parallel size 1, pipeline parallelism,
+static sequence parallelism and request boundary checkpoints. With CED
+compaction, only the encoder layers before ``ced_decoder_start`` run on
+every row: SP covers those and the boundary's row-wise normalization. The
+boundary projects local global-KV rows and gathers their 512-column values,
+plus the selected replay rows of its normalized input and residual carry.
+Selections keep the full carry gather when compact slots plus the narrow
+projection gather would cost at least as many bytes.
+
+## Rows
+
+- Collectives see ``Tp = N * ceil(T / N)`` rows; each rank owns ``L = Tp / N``
+  rows, rank r the padded rows ``[r * L, (r + 1) * L)``.
+- Kernels never see more than T rows: gathered tensors are used as ``[:T]``.
+- Reduce-scatter inputs and unreduced parts are Tp-row buffers whose pad rows
+  are zero (TileLang's zero fill).
+- The last rank's local rows can include pad rows. They stay finite and are
+  never read back into real outputs: every op on local rows is row-wise and every
+  gather keeps the first T rows. Zeros keep their values, and the routing and
+  expert work they cause, the same in every run.
+
+## Where each op runs
+
+- Local rows (L): the residual carry, mHC pre / post / post_pre / collapse,
+  attn_norm, ffn_norm, the Engram gate (``run_engram_mix``), the MoE gate and
+  top-k routing, and the final norm.
+- Gathered rows (T): the Engram table lookup (for disk column shards, each rank
+  exchanges its gathered hash columns all-to-all so it interleaves and projects
+  only its own L rows locally through ``wkv``'s column blocks; resident row
+  shards slice ``wkv`` and exchange the blocks all-to-all), attention
+  (``wq_b``, indexer, compressor, KV cache writes, sparse MLA, WO), and the
+  MoE routed and shared experts.
+- In attention layers without a compressor, and in the compressor layers
+  (ratio one and two), the row-wise front (``fused_wqa_wkv``, the q norm and
+  MXFP8 cast, the kv norm, RoPE and SWA record packing, and the local index
+  head weights) runs on local rows; only the MXFP8 q cast and 528-byte SWA
+  records are gathered, and index head weights stay rank-local. The
+  compressor projects the local rows too and gathers its 512-column values
+  (and, at ratio two, gates).
+- In encoder attention layers, ``WO-A`` projects all ``T`` rows into its
+  native MXFP8 ``o_lora`` activations, exchanges those narrower rows across
+  ranks while projecting this rank's own ``WO-B`` shard on local rows, and
+  projects the peer ``WO-B`` shards on local rows into the rank-order parts.
+- In MoE layers, ``mhc.post_pre`` already writes the local rows' MXFP8 cast and
+  the router routes the local BF16 rows; one grouped all-gather exchanges the
+  MXFP8 values, scales and local top-k routes instead of gathering the BF16
+  hidden state and casting every row again on every rank.
+
+Per decoder layer: all-gather before attention (inside
+``DeepseekV4Attention._forward``, behind the opaque attention op, which reads
+the rows from ``current()``), reduce-scatter after WO instead of the
+all-reduce, all-gather before the MoE, and reduce-scatter of the MoE output
+(shared + routed) instead of the runner's final all-reduce. The embedding
+reduce-scatters its masked partial rows (each token has one owning
+vocabulary shard, so the sum is exact); ``inputs_embeds`` are sliced. After
+the final collapse and norm, and for every aux hidden state a drafter
+consumes, the rows are gathered back to T. DSpark drafts from the aux hidden
+states only, so its pre-collapse MTP buffer is not filled under SP; other
+drafters gather it.
+
+## Unreduced results
+
+With ``UNREDUCED`` and the TP group's rank-order reduce-scatter (DS4.1's TileLang
+family on the RoCE fabric), the attention's WO output and the MoE output skip the
+sum: every rank's partial of this rank's rows is exchanged into one
+``(N, L, hidden)`` buffer, this rank's own written in place, and the decoder layer
+hands it on as ``RankOrderParts``. TileLang mHC's ``post_pre`` adds the parts in
+rank order as it loads them, the same arithmetic and the same bits as the
+rank-order reduce-scatter; any other consumer calls ``sum()``. Only real rows are
+projected into the buffers; the pad rows of the last rank's block are zeroed.
+The MoE combine (shared expert folded in) is that projection: it writes each
+rank's block straight into its slot, the other ranks' first, and the exchange of
+each slice runs under the combine of this rank's block and of the next slice.
+"""
+
+from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator
+from contextlib import contextmanager
+from contextvars import ContextVar
+from dataclasses import dataclass
+
+import torch
+
+from vllm.distributed import (
+    get_tp_group,
+    model_parallel_is_initialized,
+    tensor_model_parallel_all_gather,
+    tensor_model_parallel_all_to_all_rows,
+    tensor_model_parallel_reduce_scatter,
+)
+from vllm.logger import init_logger
+
+logger = init_logger(__name__)
+
+
+def _prefill_sp_capacity_bytes() -> int:
+    """Registered RoCE capacity used as the conservative SP floor; 0 if none."""
+    if not model_parallel_is_initialized():
+        return 0
+    dev_comm = get_tp_group().device_communicator
+    capacity = getattr(dev_comm, "all_reduce_capacity_bytes", None)
+    if capacity is not None:
+        return int(capacity)
+    comm = getattr(dev_comm, "roce_ar_comm", None) or getattr(
+        dev_comm, "b12x_ar_comm", None
+    )
+    return int(getattr(comm, "all_reduce_capacity_bytes", 0)) if comm is not None else 0
+
+
+def rows_above_bytes(limit: int, row_bytes: int, world_size: int) -> int:
+    """The fewest tokens T whose ``Tp``-row message exceeds ``limit`` bytes."""
+    padded = -(-(limit // row_bytes + 1) // world_size) * world_size
+    return padded - world_size + 1
+
+
+def resolve_min_rows(vllm_config, *, static_sequence_parallel: bool = False) -> int:
+    """The smallest forward, in tokens, that runs sequence-parallel; 0 is never.
+
+    The larger of: one token more than any decode forward (the largest CUDA
+    graph capture size, ``max_num_seqs * (1 + num_speculative_tokens)``), and
+    the fewest tokens whose padded hidden-state message exceeds the
+    registered RoCE capacity. Dispatch tuning must not also retune SP.
+    """
+    parallel = vllm_config.parallel_config
+    reason = None
+    if parallel.tensor_parallel_size <= 1:
+        reason = "tensor parallel size is 1"
+    elif static_sequence_parallel:
+        reason = "static sequence parallelism is enabled"
+    elif vllm_config.use_request_boundary_checkpoints:
+        reason = "request boundary checkpoints are enabled"
+    if reason is not None:
+        logger.info("DeepSeek V4.1 prefill sequence parallelism off: %s", reason)
+        return 0
+    capture_rows = vllm_config.compilation_config.max_cudagraph_capture_size or 0
+    limit = _prefill_sp_capacity_bytes()
+    if limit > 0:
+        model = vllm_config.model_config
+        row_bytes = model.get_hidden_size() * model.dtype.itemsize
+        tp = parallel.tensor_parallel_size
+        roce_rows = rows_above_bytes(limit, row_bytes, tp)
+        # Only captured CUDA graphs must stay on full rows past the one-shot
+        # RoCE all-reduce limit; uncaptured high-concurrency decode/verify steps
+        # above roce_rows - 1 run sequence-parallel instead of falling to PyNCCL.
+        decode_rows = max(capture_rows, tp)
+        rows = max(decode_rows + 1, roce_rows)
+        if rows > roce_rows:
+            logger.warning(
+                "max_cudagraph_capture_size (%d) exceeds one-shot RoCE all-reduce "
+                "capacity (%d rows, %d bytes); captured forwards of %d..%d rows "
+                "cannot use sequence parallelism or one-shot all-reduce",
+                capture_rows,
+                roce_rows - 1,
+                limit,
+                roce_rows,
+                rows - 1,
+            )
+    else:
+        decode_rows = max(
+            capture_rows,
+            # Every decode row the scheduler lays out, copy drafts' included.
+            vllm_config.max_decode_rows,
+            parallel.tensor_parallel_size,
+        )
+        rows = decode_rows + 1
+    logger.info(
+        "DeepSeek V4.1 prefill sequence parallelism from %d tokens "
+        "(capacity floor=%d bytes; independent of all-reduce dispatch)",
+        rows,
+        limit,
+    )
+    return rows
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class SPRows:
+    """Row layout of one sequence-parallel forward on one TP rank."""
+
+    num_tokens: int
+    world_size: int
+    rank: int
+    # Results stay unreduced (see "Unreduced results").
+    unreduced: bool = False
+
+    @property
+    def padded_rows(self) -> int:
+        """Tp: rows seen by collectives, T rounded up to a multiple of N."""
+        return -(-self.num_tokens // self.world_size) * self.world_size
+
+    @property
+    def local_rows(self) -> int:
+        """L: rows this rank owns between collectives."""
+        return self.padded_rows // self.world_size
+
+    @property
+    def start(self) -> int:
+        """First padded row owned by this rank."""
+        return self.rank * self.local_rows
+
+    @property
+    def real_rows(self) -> int:
+        """Leading local rows that are real tokens; the rest are padding."""
+        return max(0, min(self.local_rows, self.num_tokens - self.start))
+
+    def gather(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """All-gather this rank's L rows into the first T rows."""
+        x = materialize(x)
+        if x.shape[0] != self.local_rows:
+            raise ValueError(f"SP gather expects {self.local_rows} rows, got {x.shape}")
+        return tensor_model_parallel_all_gather(x, dim=0)[: self.num_tokens]
+
+    def can_gather_async(self, device: torch.device | None = None) -> bool:
+        """Whether ``gather_many_async`` can run a grouped PyNCCL gather on ``_side_stream``."""
+        if not model_parallel_is_initialized() or _tp_pynccl_comm() is None:
+            return False
+        if not torch.cuda.is_available() or torch.cuda.is_current_stream_capturing():
+            return False
+        return device is None or device.type == "cuda"
+
+    def can_gather_mxfp8_async(self, device: torch.device | None = None) -> bool:
+        """Whether ``gather_mxfp8_async`` can run asynchronously without bypassing monkeypatches."""
+        return (
+            type(self).gather_mxfp8 is _DEFAULT_GATHER_MXFP8
+            and "gather_mxfp8" not in self.__dict__
+            and self.can_gather_async(device)
+        )
+
+    def _prepare_gather_many(
+        self, *tensors: torch.Tensor, padded_rows: tuple[int, ...] = ()
+    ) -> tuple[list[torch.Tensor], tuple[int, ...], object | None]:
+        inputs = []
+        for x in tensors:
+            x = materialize(x)
+            if x.shape[0] != self.local_rows:
+                raise ValueError(
+                    f"SP gather expects {self.local_rows} rows, got {x.shape}"
+                )
+            inputs.append(x)
+        limits = padded_rows + (self.num_tokens,) * (len(inputs) - len(padded_rows))
+        comm = (
+            getattr(get_tp_group().device_communicator, "pynccl_comm", None)
+            if model_parallel_is_initialized()
+            else None
+        )
+        if comm is not None and getattr(comm, "disabled", False):
+            comm = None
+        return inputs, limits, comm
+
+    def _launch_pynccl_gather(
+        self,
+        inputs: list[torch.Tensor],
+        limits: tuple[int, ...],
+        comm,
+        *,
+        stream: torch.cuda.Stream | None = None,
+        ready_event: torch.cuda.Event | None = None,
+        done_event: torch.cuda.Event | None = None,
+    ) -> tuple[torch.Tensor, ...]:
+        outs = []
+        pairs = []
+        for x, rows in zip(inputs, limits):
+            inp = x.contiguous()
+            alloc_rows = max(self.padded_rows, rows)
+            out = torch.empty(
+                (alloc_rows, *inp.shape[1:]), dtype=inp.dtype, device=inp.device
+            )
+
+            outs.append(out[:rows])
+            pairs.append((out[: self.padded_rows], inp))
+        if stream is not None:
+            main = torch.cuda.current_stream(inputs[0].device)
+            if ready_event is not None:
+                ready_event.record(main)
+                stream.wait_event(ready_event)
+            else:
+                stream.wait_stream(main)
+        comm.group_start()
+        for dst, src in pairs:
+            if stream is None:
+                comm.all_gather(dst, src)
+            else:
+                comm.all_gather(dst, src, stream=stream)
+        comm.group_end()
+        if stream is not None and done_event is not None:
+            done_event.record(stream)
+        return tuple(outs)
+
+    def gather_many(
+        self, *tensors: torch.Tensor, padded_rows: tuple[int, ...] = ()
+    ) -> tuple[torch.Tensor, ...]:
+        """All-gather several L-row tensors into their first T rows (or ``padded_rows``
+        when given for a tensor) in one grouped PyNCCL collective when available."""
+        inputs, limits, comm = self._prepare_gather_many(
+            *tensors, padded_rows=padded_rows
+        )
+        if comm is None:
+            outs = []
+            for x, rows in zip(inputs, limits):
+                gathered = tensor_model_parallel_all_gather(x, dim=0)
+                if rows > gathered.shape[0]:
+                    padded = x.new_empty((rows, *x.shape[1:]))
+                    padded[: gathered.shape[0]].copy_(gathered)
+                    outs.append(padded)
+                else:
+                    outs.append(gathered[:rows])
+            return tuple(outs)
+        return self._launch_pynccl_gather(inputs, limits, comm)
+
+    def gather_many_async(
+        self, *tensors: torch.Tensor, padded_rows: tuple[int, ...] = ()
+    ) -> tuple[tuple[torch.Tensor, ...], Callable[[], None]]:
+        """Start a grouped PyNCCL all-gather on ``_side_stream`` and return ``(outs, wait_fn)``."""
+        inputs, limits, comm = self._prepare_gather_many(
+            *tensors, padded_rows=padded_rows
+        )
+        if not inputs or comm is None or not self.can_gather_async(inputs[0].device):
+            return self.gather_many(*tensors, padded_rows=padded_rows), (lambda: None)
+        inputs = [x.contiguous() for x in inputs]
+        device = inputs[0].device
+        side = _side_stream(device)
+        ready_ev, done_ev = _next_gather_events(device)
+        outs = self._launch_pynccl_gather(
+            inputs,
+            limits,
+            comm,
+            stream=side,
+            ready_event=ready_ev,
+            done_event=done_ev,
+        )
+        # Keep both contiguous sources and outputs alive until main waits on done_ev
+        # so the caching allocator cannot recycle them on main mid-transfer.
+        held: tuple[list[torch.Tensor], tuple[torch.Tensor, ...]] | None = (
+            inputs,
+            outs,
+        )
+        waited = False
+
+        def wait() -> None:
+            nonlocal waited, held
+            if not waited:
+                waited = True
+                torch.cuda.current_stream(device).wait_event(done_ev)
+                held = None
+
+        return outs, wait
+
+    def gather_mxfp8(self, x_q, *extra: torch.Tensor):
+        """All-gather this rank's L-row ``MXFP8Rows`` (and any ``extra`` L-row
+        tensors, such as local top-k routes) in one grouped collective, returning
+        ``(MXFP8Rows, *extra_gathered)``."""
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang.linear import MXFP8Rows, mxfp8_rows
+
+        local = self.local_rows
+        if x_q.rows.shape[0] != local:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"SP MXFP8 gather expects {local} rows, got {x_q.rows.shape}"
+            )
+        rows_q = mxfp8_rows(self.num_tokens)
+        values, scales, *rest = self.gather_many(
+            x_q.values[:local],
+            x_q.scales[:local],
+            *extra,
+            padded_rows=(rows_q, rows_q),
+        )
+        rows = torch.empty(
+            (self.num_tokens, *x_q.rows.shape[1:]),
+            dtype=x_q.rows.dtype,
+            device=x_q.rows.device,
+        )
+        return (MXFP8Rows(rows, values, scales), *rest)
+
+    def gather_mxfp8_async(self, x_q, *extra: torch.Tensor):
+        """Asynchronous ``gather_mxfp8`` returning ``((MXFP8Rows, *extra), wait_fn)``."""
+        if not self.can_gather_mxfp8_async(x_q.rows.device):
+            return self.gather_mxfp8(x_q, *extra), (lambda: None)
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang.linear import MXFP8Rows, mxfp8_rows
+
+        local = self.local_rows
+        if x_q.rows.shape[0] != local:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"SP MXFP8 gather expects {local} rows, got {x_q.rows.shape}"
+            )
+        rows_q = mxfp8_rows(self.num_tokens)
+        (values, scales, *rest), wait = self.gather_many_async(
+            x_q.values[:local],
+            x_q.scales[:local],
+            *extra,
+            padded_rows=(rows_q, rows_q),
+        )
+        rows = torch.empty(
+            (self.num_tokens, *x_q.rows.shape[1:]),
+            dtype=x_q.rows.dtype,
+            device=x_q.rows.device,
+        )
+        return (MXFP8Rows(rows, values, scales), *rest), wait
+
+    def reduce_scatter(self, padded: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """Sum a zero-padded Tp-row buffer over the ranks into this rank's rows."""
+        if padded.shape[0] != self.padded_rows:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"SP reduce-scatter expects {self.padded_rows} rows, got {padded.shape}"
+            )
+        return tensor_model_parallel_reduce_scatter(padded, dim=0)
+
+    def exchange_rows(self, local: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """Every rank's column block of this rank's rows of a column-parallel product
+        of all T rows, ``local`` being this rank's block of every row: ``[N, L, C]``,
+        [s] from rank s, so the blocks side by side in rank order are the columns an
+        all-gather gives. An all-to-all of each rank's real rows: 1/N of the
+        all-gather's bytes, no copy. Rows past this rank's real rows are not written."""
+        if local.shape[0] != self.num_tokens:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"SP row exchange expects {self.num_tokens} rows, got {local.shape}"
+            )
+        return tensor_model_parallel_all_to_all_rows(local, self.local_rows)
+
+    def project_exchange_rows(
+        self,
+        project,
+        row_shape: tuple[int, ...],
+        dtype: torch.dtype,
+        device: torch.device,
+        slices: int = 1,
+        then=None,
+    ) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """Every rank's column block of this rank's rows of a column-parallel product
+        of all T rows, ``[N, L, *row_shape]``, [s] from rank s.
+
+        ``project(start, stop, out)`` writes this rank's column block of rows
+        ``start:stop`` into ``out``. Each slice's peer blocks are projected into a send
+        buffer and exchanged into ``out[:, lo:hi]`` on a side stream (``copy_self=False``)
+        while this rank's own block of the slice is projected straight into
+        ``out[rank, lo : lo + real]`` without allocating a full-row intermediate or
+        copying the self-block. ``then()`` runs on the current stream after the last
+        projection, before the last exchange is awaited. Rows past this rank's real
+        rows are not written.
+
+        Under the one-shot RoCE policy, one slice is one full-row projection,
+        ``then()`` and the TP group's row exchange (``exchange_rows``, one-shot RoCE
+        when the rows fit, else PyNCCL); two or more slices take the PyNCCL
+        pipeline above."""
+        local, world, tokens = self.local_rows, self.world_size, self.num_tokens
+        comm = _tp_pynccl_comm()
+        slices = max(slices, 1)
+        roce_rows = (
+            getattr(_tp_roce_comm(), "should_all_to_all_rows", None) is not None
+        )
+        if comm is None or (roce_rows and slices == 1):
+            local_kv = torch.empty((tokens, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+            if tokens:
+                project(0, tokens, local_kv)
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+            return self.exchange_rows(local_kv)
+        out = torch.empty((world, local, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+        send = torch.empty((world * local, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+        bounds = [local * i // slices for i in range(slices + 1)]
+        use_cuda_streams = device.type == "cuda" and torch.cuda.is_available()
+        main = torch.cuda.current_stream(device) if use_cuda_streams else None
+        side = _side_stream(device) if use_cuda_streams else None
+        try:
+            for lo, hi in zip(bounds, bounds[1:]):
+                slice_rows = hi - lo
+                if slice_rows == 0:
+                    continue
+                send_slice = send[world * lo : world * hi].view(
+                    world, slice_rows, *row_shape
+                )
+                slice_total = 0
+                for owner in range(world):
+                    real = max(0, min(hi, tokens - owner * local) - lo)
+                    slice_total += real
+                    if owner != self.rank and real:
+                        start = owner * local + lo
+                        project(start, start + real, send_slice[owner, :real])
+                if slice_total:
+                    flat_send = send_slice.view(world * slice_rows, *row_shape)[
+                        :slice_total
+                    ]
+                    if use_cuda_streams:
+                        side.wait_stream(main)
+                        with torch.cuda.stream(side):
+                            comm.all_to_all_rows(
+                                out[:, lo:hi],
+                                flat_send,
+                                slice_rows,
+                                stream=side,
+                                copy_self=False,
+                            )
+                    else:
+                        comm.all_to_all_rows(
+                            out[:, lo:hi],
+                            flat_send,
+                            slice_rows,
+                            stream=None,
+                            copy_self=False,
+                        )
+                real_me = max(0, min(hi, tokens - self.rank * local) - lo)
+                if real_me:
+                    start = self.rank * local + lo
+                    project(start, start + real_me, out[self.rank, lo : lo + real_me])
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+        finally:
+            if use_cuda_streams:
+                # send and out are freed only after this wait, on this stream.
+                main.wait_stream(side)
+        return out
+
+    def empty_padded(
+        self, row_shape: tuple[int, ...], dtype: torch.dtype, device: torch.device
+    ) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """A Tp-row buffer whose pad rows (T and beyond) are zero."""
+        padded = torch.empty((self.padded_rows, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+        padded[self.num_tokens :].zero_()
+        return padded
+
+    def local_slice(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """This rank's L rows of a T-row tensor; pad rows are zero."""
+        if x.shape[0] != self.num_tokens:
+            raise ValueError(f"SP slice expects {self.num_tokens} rows, got {x.shape}")
+        real = self.real_rows
+        rows = x[self.start : self.start + real]
+        if real == self.local_rows:
+            return rows
+        local = x.new_zeros((self.local_rows, *x.shape[1:]))
+        local[:real].copy_(rows)
+        return local
+
+    def project_reduce_scatter(
+        self,
+        project,
+        row_shape: tuple[int, ...],
+        dtype: torch.dtype,
+        device: torch.device,
+        slices: int = 1,
+        then=None,
+        per_block: bool = False,
+    ) -> torch.Tensor:
+        """This rank's L rows of the sum over ranks of a T-row projection.
+
+        ``project(start, stop, out)`` writes rows ``start:stop`` of the projection
+        into ``out``. With ``slices`` > 1 each rank's block is projected in that many
+        pieces, every piece of every block into one contiguous buffer, and each
+        piece is reduce-scattered on a side stream while the next is projected.
+        A projection whose rows do not depend on one another reduces to the same
+        bits as one projection and one reduce-scatter. ``then()`` runs on the
+        current stream after the last projection, before the last reduce-scatter
+        is awaited.
+
+        With ``unreduced`` rows the result is every rank's unreduced partial of
+        this rank's rows instead, ``(N, L, *row_shape)``; see "Unreduced results".
+        Block by block (``per_block``, or ``slices`` > 1), each rank's block is
+        written with its own call, this rank's straight into its slot, and each
+        slice's exchange starts on the side stream once the other ranks' blocks
+        are written, under this rank's own and the next slice (for writers that
+        cost nothing per call, such as the MoE combine). Otherwise one call
+        writes every row and this rank's block is copied into its slot (a
+        projection reads its weights once).
+        """
+        if self.unreduced:
+            return self._project_exchange(
+                project, row_shape, dtype, device, slices, then, per_block
+            )
+        if slices <= 1:
+            padded = self.empty_padded(row_shape, dtype, device)
+            project(0, self.num_tokens, padded[: self.num_tokens])
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+            return self.reduce_scatter(padded)
+        local, world, tokens = self.local_rows, self.world_size, self.num_tokens
+        out = torch.empty((local, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+        bounds = [local * i // slices for i in range(slices + 1)]
+        main = torch.cuda.current_stream(device)
+        side = _side_stream(device)
+        pieces: list[torch.Tensor] = []
+        try:
+            for lo, hi in zip(bounds, bounds[1:]):
+                if hi == lo:
+                    continue
+                piece = torch.empty(
+                    (world, hi - lo, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device
+                )
+                pieces.append(piece)
+                for owner in range(world):
+                    start, stop = owner * local + lo, owner * local + hi
+                    real = max(0, min(stop, tokens) - start)
+                    if real:
+                        project(start, start + real, piece[owner, :real])
+                    if real < hi - lo:
+                        piece[owner, real:].zero_()
+                side.wait_stream(main)
+                with torch.cuda.stream(side):
+                    reduced = tensor_model_parallel_reduce_scatter(
+                        piece.view(world * (hi - lo), *row_shape), dim=0
+                    )
+                    out[lo:hi].copy_(reduced)
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+        finally:
+            main.wait_stream(side)
+        return out
+
+    def _project_exchange(
+        self, project, row_shape, dtype, device, slices, then, per_block=False
+    ):
+        """``project_reduce_scatter`` without the sum: each rank's block goes into
+        its slot of one send buffer, this rank's own straight into its slot of
+        the parts, and the chunks are exchanged into the parts. Block by block,
+        each slice is exchanged on the side stream once the other ranks' blocks
+        of it are projected, while this rank's own block and the next slice
+        are."""
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang import columns
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang.collectives import exchange_into
+
+        local, world, tokens = self.local_rows, self.world_size, self.num_tokens
+        send = torch.empty((world, local, *row_shape), dtype=dtype, device=device)
+        parts = torch.empty_like(send)
+        slices = max(slices, 1)
+        if slices == 1 and not per_block:
+            flat = send.view(world * local, *row_shape)
+            project(0, tokens, flat[:tokens])
+            columns.zero_(flat[tokens:])
+            parts[self.rank].copy_(send[self.rank])
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+            self.exchange_into(send, parts)
+            return parts
+
+        def write(owner, lo, hi):
+            dest = parts if owner == self.rank else send
+            start, stop = owner * local + lo, owner * local + hi
+            real = max(0, min(stop, tokens) - start)
+            if real:
+                project(start, start + real, dest[owner, lo : lo + real])
+            columns.zero_(dest[owner, lo + real : hi])
+
+        bounds = [local * i // slices for i in range(slices + 1)]
+        main = torch.cuda.current_stream(device)
+        side = _side_stream(device)
+        try:
+            for lo, hi in zip(bounds, bounds[1:]):
+                if hi == lo:
+                    continue
+                for owner in range(world):
+                    if owner != self.rank:
+                        write(owner, lo, hi)
+                side.wait_stream(main)
+                with torch.cuda.stream(side):
+                    self.exchange_into(send[:, lo:hi], parts[:, lo:hi])
+                write(self.rank, lo, hi)
+            if then is not None:
+                then()
+        finally:
+            # send and parts are freed only after this wait, on this stream.
+            main.wait_stream(side)
+        return parts
+
+    def exchange_into(self, send: torch.Tensor, recv) -> None:
+        """Exchange ``send[peer]`` into ``recv[peer]`` for every peer ``!= rank``."""
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang.collectives import exchange_into
+
+        dev_comm = get_tp_group().device_communicator
+        comm = dev_comm.pynccl_comm
+        roce_comm = _tp_roce_comm()
+        if (
+            isinstance(recv, torch.Tensor)
+            and roce_comm is not None
+            and _roce_should_exchange(roce_comm, send, recv)
+        ):
+            roce_comm.exchange_into(send, recv)
+            return
+        exchange_into(comm, send, recv, self.rank, self.world_size)
+
+    def exchange_many_into(self, *pairs) -> None:
+        """Exchange multiple `(send, recv)` pairs in one collective group when possible."""
+        if not pairs:
+            return
+        if (
+            len(pairs) == 1
+            or not model_parallel_is_initialized()
+            or type(self).exchange_into is not _DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_INTO
+            or "exchange_into" in self.__dict__
+        ):
+            for send, recv in pairs:
+                self.exchange_into(send, recv)
+            return
+        from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang import collectives
+
+        dev_comm = get_tp_group().device_communicator
+        comm = dev_comm.pynccl_comm
+        roce_comm = _tp_roce_comm()
+        nccl_pairs = []
+        for send, recv in pairs:
+            if (
+                isinstance(recv, torch.Tensor)
+                and roce_comm is not None
+                and _roce_should_exchange(roce_comm, send, recv)
+            ):
+                roce_comm.exchange_into(send, recv)
+            else:
+                nccl_pairs.append((send, recv))
+        if not nccl_pairs:
+            return
+        if (
+            len(nccl_pairs) == 1
+            or (self.world_size == 4 and collectives.ring4_relay())
+            or not hasattr(comm, "group_start")
+        ):
+            for send, recv in nccl_pairs:
+                collectives.exchange_into(
+                    comm, send, recv, self.rank, self.world_size
+                )
+            return
+        comm.group_start()
+        for send, recv in nccl_pairs:
+            for peer in range(self.world_size):
+                if peer != self.rank:
+                    collectives._send(comm, send[peer], peer)
+                    collectives._recv(comm, recv[peer], peer)
+        comm.group_end()
+
+
+_DEFAULT_GATHER_MXFP8 = SPRows.gather_mxfp8
+_DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_INTO = SPRows.exchange_into
+SPRows._DEFAULT_GATHER_MXFP8 = _DEFAULT_GATHER_MXFP8
+SPRows._DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_INTO = _DEFAULT_EXCHANGE_INTO
+
+
+# The attention's WO projection is reduce-scattered in two slices from this many
+# tokens, so half its reduce-scatter runs under the other half's projection.
+WO_SLICE_TOKENS = 2048
+
+
+def wo_slices(num_tokens: int) -> int:
+    """Slices of a sequence-parallel WO projection of ``num_tokens`` tokens."""
+    return 2 if num_tokens >= WO_SLICE_TOKENS else 1
+
+
+# The Engram projection's row exchange runs in two slices from this many tokens,
+# so each slice's peer exchange runs under this rank's own block and the next slice
+# once the per-slice projection GEMM is large enough to amortize weight streaming.
+ENGRAM_SLICE_TOKENS = 6144
+
+
+def engram_slices(num_tokens: int) -> int:
